  "label": "Firework as Celebratory Object",
  "description": "Fireworks are universally recognized symbols of celebration, festivity, and public joy — often used in national holidays, New Year’s Eve, and other communal events. Their association with positive, non-violent spectacle is central to the meme’s irony. The meme equates the celebratory object with the violent label, creating a satirical contrast.",
